ences so you  should definitely pause it to see how  many you recognize we can tell you right  now that you can find references to at  least five other elderly cartoon  characters in a single shot seriously  we're totally amazed by all these  shoutouts to some of our favorite  characters shows and artists of the pop  culture but the loud house also pay  homage to other icons Shakespeare now  here's something kids these days  definitely would notice when you think  of Shakespeare you probably think of the  famous to be or not to be quote but  there was so much more to this amazing  writer in fact you can find several very  subtle Shakespeare quotes in our  favorite Nickelodeon show the loud house  made a reference to Shakespeare on two  separate occasions the first time was in  the episode called spell it out where we  see Lucy use a spell book to teach her  siblings a lesson because she's annoyed  at them we've all been there Lucy but  did you notice the spell she's been  using she says things like lizards leg  and owlets wing which is directly taken  from Macbeth's act for what a cool  shout-out and if you've been watching  season 3 you can also find a Shakespeare  reference in the episode called white  hair we see Warren the rabbit read  rabbit version of Shakespeare called  shakes hare this of course is a play on  Shakespeare and well rabbits who would  have thought that Shakespeare's work  would have such influence even more than  400 years after his publications and  Lucy is just the perfect character to  pay homage to this iconic writer  spongebob the shout outs to spongebob  have probably been the most obvious in  the loud house but one of them gets  frequently missed season 1 episode 1 of  the lob house already starts with the  bang but you might want to rewatch it  because while you were focusing  the characters themselves and trying to  get to know them a lot of things happen  in the background this very subtle  reference occurs for a split second so  it's